Subject: Cantor Windows Topology Attribute and Name Policy

Description: Proposed fail-closed M2B profile for Windows entry attributes, per-directory case behavior, and path components. This is research, not activation authority.

& [PolicyIdentity] is a pre-activation strict-profile proposal
  + [policy_uuid] is 2563a009-a96e-4201-b02d-6f04bd3edc78
  + [captured_at] is 2026-07-30
  + [profile] is cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + [status] is proposed_pending_fixture_proof

@ [formation] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Scanner.sop
@ [unsafe_seam] C:\Project\Cantor\narrative\research\Cantor_Windows_Topology_Unsafe_Seam_Review_2026-07-30.sop
@ [Microsoft_attributes] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/file-attribute-constants
@ [Microsoft_names] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/fileio/naming-a-file
@ [Microsoft_case_sensitivity] https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/case-sensitivity

& [BenignAttributeSet] is the only combinable profile set
  + [READONLY] is 0x00000001
  + [HIDDEN] is 0x00000002
  + [SYSTEM] is 0x00000004
  + [ARCHIVE] is 0x00000020
  + [NOT_CONTENT_INDEXED] is 0x00002000
  + [combined_mask] is 0x00002027
  + [reason] is these bits do not introduce alias traversal, deferred retrieval, alternate content, sparse allocation, encryption, compression, virtualization, or unsupported object behavior

& [DirectoryAttributeRule] is exact
  + [DIRECTORY] is 0x00000010 and must be set
  + [allowed_mask] is DIRECTORY plus any BenignAttributeSet bit, numerically 0x00002037
  + [NORMAL] must be absent because Microsoft defines it as valid only alone
  + [unknown_bit] rejects
  + [kind_mismatch] rejects

& [RegularAttributeRule] is exact
  + [DIRECTORY] must be absent
  + [normal_shape] is exactly FILE_ATTRIBUTE_NORMAL 0x00000080
  + [marked_shape] is one or more BenignAttributeSet bits and no other bit
  + [zero] rejects because it does not prove a valid returned attribute shape
  + [unknown_bit] rejects
  + [kind_mismatch] rejects

& [RejectedBehaviorBits] are closed for profile 0.1
  + [DEVICE] is 0x00000040
  + [TEMPORARY] is 0x00000100
  + [SPARSE_FILE] is 0x00000200
  + [REPARSE_POINT] is 0x00000400
  + [COMPRESSED] is 0x00000800
  + [OFFLINE] is 0x00001000
  + [ENCRYPTED] is 0x00004000
  + [INTEGRITY_STREAM] is 0x00008000
  + [VIRTUAL] is 0x00010000
  + [NO_SCRUB_DATA] is 0x00020000
  + [EA_or_RECALL_ON_OPEN] is 0x00040000
  + [PINNED] is 0x00080000
  + [UNPINNED] is 0x00100000
  + [RECALL_ON_DATA_ACCESS] is 0x00400000
  + [reason] is initial reconstruction and containment semantics are not proven for any of these behaviors
  - never: admit a behavior bit merely because ordinary logical reads happened to succeed

& [CaseSensitivityRule] is per directory
  + [query] is GetFileInformationByHandleEx FileCaseSensitiveInfo on the already opened directory handle
  + [structure] is FILE_CASE_SENSITIVE_INFO with unsigned Flags
  + [admission] requires Flags equal to zero
  + [nonzero] rejects both the known case-sensitive-directory bit and any future unknown bit
  + [why] is Windows tools can otherwise address case-distinct entries inconsistently and Git interpretation can diverge
  + [Git_reconciliation] still requires exact case-preserved path equality between physical and Git inventories

& [ComponentCharacterRule] is strict
  + [encoding] is valid Unicode round-tripped from exact UTF-16 without replacement
  + [length] is nonzero and within the volume maximum-component length and Cantor policy bound
  + [forbidden] is NUL, U+0001 through U+001F, less-than, greater-than, colon, quote, slash, backslash, vertical-bar, question-mark, and asterisk
  + [terminal] rejects a trailing space or period
  + [navigation] rejects dot and dot-dot
  + [Git_control] rejects .git under ordinal ASCII case-insensitive comparison
  + [normalization] preserves exact code points and does not silently normalize Unicode

& [ReservedDeviceRule] is stem-based and case-insensitive
  + [stem] is the component before its first period
  + [fixed] rejects CON, PRN, AUX, and NUL
  + [numbered] rejects COM1 through COM9 and LPT1 through LPT9
  + [superscript] rejects COM and LPT followed by ISO-8859-1 superscript 1, 2, or 3
  + [extension] does not make a reserved stem safe
  + [reason] is Win32 can interpret these as devices rather than ordinary candidate content

& [OrderingRule] is evidence order not path equivalence
  + [canonical_order] is exact UTF-8 bytes of slash-normalized relative paths
  + [uniqueness] is exact byte uniqueness plus exact Git reconciliation
  + [case] does not use locale-sensitive lowercase or uppercase transformations
  + [case_sensitive_directory] is rejected before ordering

& [UnresolvedBeforeFreeze] remains blocking
  + [NORMAL_observation] target-host fixtures must confirm FileAttributeTagInfo returns NORMAL alone for an otherwise unmarked regular file
  + [directory_READONLY] is allowed as an observed benign bit even though Microsoft says it is not honored for directories; the fixture must confirm no special folder behavior
  + [Unicode] visually confusable or canonically equivalent distinct components are preserved, but any higher-level semantic collision policy is not yet specified
  + [Git_modes] executable-bit truth comes from exact Git inventory and must not be inferred from these Windows attributes

& [AuthorityEffect] is none
  + [next_step] is incorporate only after source selection, fixture design, and an M2B satisfaction signature
  - never: cite this policy as scanner, dependency, unsafe, fixture, sandbox, mutation, seal, cleanup, or promotion authority
